+  {"kind": "spec", "item": "Phase 3 JS: replace step 1.3 in ui/handlers.js (line 175) — swap npm install -g @codemieai/code with a codemie --version probe against the PATH-injected binary", "status": "fail", "notes": "ui/handlers.js is not in the diff; step 1.3 is not replaced"}
+]
+```
+
+- **AC1 / AC2 — VM validation not performed**: Phase 3 prerequisites are incomplete (`tauri.macos.conf.json` not created, `ui/handlers.js` not modified), and `SPIKE_RESULT.md` contains no Phase 3 section. Neither `codemie --version` nor `codemie install [agent]` has been validated on a clean `aarch64` VM.
+- **AC3 — SPIKE_RESULT.md missing Phase 3 content**: Phase 1 and Phase 2 are documented with the `pkg` invocation and exit code. Because neither phase halted early, the spec requires a Phase 3 section recording `codesign` output and verbatim VM stdout/stderr for both commands; that section is absent.
+- **AC5 — tauri.macos.conf.json not created**: The spec requires `src-tauri/tauri.macos.conf.json` with `externalBin: ["../assets/bin/codemie"]`, `bundle.macOS.signingIdentity`, and `[throwaway]` comments on every spike-specific key. The file does not appear in the diff.
+- **Spec Phase 3 Rust — hardcoded PATH separator**: `inject_bundled_bin_path` at `pathman.rs:276` (diff line +107) constructs the new PATH value with a literal `:` separator (`format!("{}:{}", dir.display(), current)`). The file defines `PATH_SEP` as `';'` on Windows and `':'` elsewhere; the new function ignores it, producing a malformed `PATH` on Windows targets.
+- **Spec Phase 3 JS — handlers.js step 1.2 not short-circuited**: `ui/handlers.js` lines 109–149 (the system Node check/download step) are unchanged; the bundled binary path will trigger a system Node probe it does not need.
+- **Spec Phase 3 JS — handlers.js step 1.3 not replaced**: `ui/handlers.js` line 175 still invokes `npm install -g @codemieai/code` rather than a `codemie --version` probe against the PATH-injected binary.
